   Curry-Howard analogue of Sigma types</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?DependentConjunction]" target="latin:/?DependentConjunction"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/dependent_pl.mmt#184.6.0:210.6.26"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?DependentConjunctionND]" target="latin:/?DependentConjunctionND"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/dependent_pl.mmt#288.11.0:316.11.28"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/dependent_pl.mmt#535.18.0:762.19.120"/></metadata>Disjunction where the second disjunct's well-formedness may depend on the falsity of the first disjunct
   Curry-Howard analogue of an unusual union type where the second argument is only considered if the first one is empty</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?DependentDisjunction]" target="latin:/?DependentDisjunction"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/dependent_pl.mmt#765.20.0:791.20.26"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?DependentDisjunctionND]" target="latin:/?DependentDisjunctionND"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/dependent_pl.mmt#875.25.0:903.25.28"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/dependent_pl.mmt#1136.32.0:1267.33.37"/></metadata>Implication where the implicate's well-formedness may depend on the truth of the implicant
